<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  WildPlants_Webwork.xml                    UtinniPatches — new file 2026-09-25
  ============================================================================

  WEBWORK_FLORA_ROSTER_1. Injects the genuine canon Star Wars plant
  `Plant_TookeTrap_Wild` onto RM_Webwork's wildPlants, additively and kept at
  low commonality, per the biome's own sitting record
  (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/webwork_owner_and_nest_2026-09-23.md §6
  ruling 8, 2026-09-24 question card): "`Plant_TookeTrap_Wild` is KEPT LOW via
  a Utinni `WildPlants_Webwork` patch, with the invented `RM_Kessaroth` as the
  free tier's snap-trap. Canon injects on top; the free mod stands whole."

  WHY THIS FILE HAS TO EXIST. §7 Q11 (owner, 2026-09-22): a RM_-tier def may
  never name Star Wars content, and "tooke-trap" is genuine canon IP (Q11a,
  named in the tier law itself as the worked example) — it cannot sit in
  RM_Webwork's own wildPlants, unlike the 16 invented rows in
  RM_WebworkFlora.xml. `WildAnimals_Pyrelands.xml` / `WildAnimals_Webwork.xml`
  are the shape this copies, applied here to a plant instead of an animal.

  Commonality kept at 0.3 — the same value the frozen `RUT_Webwork.xml` twin
  has always carried this row at (its own wildPlants block, unedited, frozen
  2026-09-25) — matching the ruling's "kept low," not raised or lowered by
  this patch. `RM_Kessaroth` (RM_WebworkFlora.xml) ships in RM_Webwork itself
  as the free tier's own snap-trap; this canon row is a second, additive jaw
  in the thicket for campaign players only, never a substitute (Q11a).

  ⚠️ A patch that matches nothing logs nothing (PatchOperationConditional
  returns true on no match) — validate against the live def dump and the full
  active mod set before trusting a clean run as proof the row landed.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- Star Wars Animal Collection (Continued)'s own bare defName — same donor
       mod as the Webwork's canon fauna cast (WildAnimals_Webwork.xml). -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="mlie.starwarsanimalcollection">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Webwork"]/wildPlants</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Webwork"]/wildPlants</xpath>
      <value>
        <Plant_TookeTrap_Wild>0.3</Plant_TookeTrap_Wild>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
